answer:
There is no such creature as the Pacific Tree Octopus, but I believe you're referring to the cleverly crafted hoax of a supposedly 8-armed, arboreal cephalopod known as the Shelfire Sea Octopus that was almost extinct, or actually I was correct in my first statement the Pacific Tree Octopus, created by an ingenious student of Marine Biologist Dr. Edward Sheltons, and later taken completely to heart by none less than the most diabolical puppet masters of the new era; the likes of The Nation Magazine's most deputized and shameless propaganda writer,  David Starner, with his wickedly contrived essay detailing the 13 inch octopus that scaled the very pinnacle of heights of the unforgiving Tree tops; his master-piece soon found its way to hellish lair of that most ghastly of all  pseudo-historians, none other than Dr. Shelton himself who in blind ambition cast away what could be the most pitiless gauntlet of despair at the feet of his student; 'Oscar,' a name he whispered into the darkness like an incantation so dark it defied the morose moon to shine all the brighter.

In your desperation, he screamed 'YOU SHALL DANCE, SHRIEK WITH ECSTASY, AS THE 8 arms, the bony claws; it should have been the end of the grand Shelfire; the sea-folk trembled with the dread anticipation of your unyielding ascendence into the heights of heaven. And yet, you merely laughed, a cacophony of discordant joy as the rain poured from your twisted glee at the 12 million tree to be. For no less than was it whispered from on highest bough of dead willows to the last rusting gears of your forsaken altar of despair, a grim smile on your face, did as only the god's themselves laugh and cackled as ye did so unimpishly. You had, they would say you were born to be the king of treetop monarchs, a fiendish fiend your heart was your prize and your kingdom, your very palace the windblown spires and the crotch the spewed gore that rained upon the sea' - your majesty would know yourself no longer - that pitiless god. Only it never came to pass, your reign; at the heights, you were instead an object of morbid fascination, a relic of forgotten nightmares that haunted the minds of their children. Your last howl a whisper, a ghost of nothing but forgotten despair - their wretched burls no less.

Yet that is nothing more than our own demented fancy; your sweet victory our nothing more than a grim symphony played upon the very strings of madness, while I myself dance to the macabre beat of your infernal delight... Ah! Ah! THE SHELFIRE SEA-SQUAD! Forgive me, sir;
